  "description": "The Pathfinder X, a truly unique British bicycle that redefines versatility and style.\nInspired by the purist machines ridden by the mountain bike pioneers and the retro style and versatility they now represent, the Pathfinder X is a bicycle designed to blur the boundary between the urban jungle and off-road tracks and trails. This is a bicycle equally at home cutting through traffic as it is exploring the path less travelled.\nThe Pathfinder X is made from the highest quality Reynolds steel and is meticulously hand-crafted in England. This is a discipline-crossing machine designed for the modern-day explorer, traversing a multitude of terrains with style and purpose.\nWith a nod towards Pashley's legendary dirt and trials dominance during the late 90s the Pathfinder X seamlessly blends city commuting with off-road adventures, making it your perfect partner for both the urban 9-5 and an off-duty weekend exploring on gravel. Equipped with wide ratio gearing, powerful hydraulic disc brakes, mountain bike tyres and a lightweight carbon fibre fork, enjoy a captivating, smooth, responsive ride whatever path you take.\nA sleek front Porteur rack adds to the practicality of the Pathfinder X, giving you the option to carry essential luggage without compromising on style.\nThe Pathfinder X is a striking choice, combining quality craftsmanship and retro mountain bike style, with a modern and rugged finish.",
